<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Najib Razak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Najib Razak is a Malaysian politician, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-razak-hussein">Tun Abdul Razak</a>, who was the sixth prime minister of Malaysia from 2009 to 2018. His government was engulfed by the 1MDB scandal, in which billions of dollars were taken from a state investment fund, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> lost power in 2018. He was convicted of corruption in 2020 and imprisoned in 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/najib-razak.jpg" alt="Najib Razak" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Malaysia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Najib_Razak_2008-08-21.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
